    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this is a provisional automated ruling.\n\nTHE MEASUREMENTS. The GPS trace for this trip (EV-GPS-00104, weight 1.0) measures 34.17 km between pickup and dropoff. POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern; the 34.2 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00104) is a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement. The booked optimal route was 27.1 km, so the measured excess is 7.07 km, or 26.09% of optimal — above both the 20% and the 0.8 km tests, so a deviation is established under POL-RD-01.\n\nTHE CLOSURE EXPLAINS MOST OF IT. The driver's account of an accident is corroborated by the LTA DataMall advisory ADV-20260716-007 (EV-ADVIS-00104-01, weight 1.0): a HIGH-severity multi-vehicle accident on the PIE towards Tuas after Eunos Link exit — the expressway the booked optimal route uses ('PIE westbound throughout') — active 20:02–21:35, which covers the trip, with the trace showing the vehicle leaving the PIE at Bedok North Ave 4 ahead of the blocked segment and rejoining on the AYE. All three limbs of POL-RD-03 are met. Exoneration is capped: justified excess = min(7.07 km, 1.30 × (30.1 − 27.1) + 1.00) = min(7.07, 4.90) = 4.90 km, so the closure-adjusted optimal route is 32.00 km at 40.1 minutes.\n\nTHE REFUND. POL-RD-03 provides that excess beyond the cap is not exonerated and is refunded under POL-RD-02 computed against the closure-adjusted optimal route. Run on the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00104, weight 1.0; fare_model METERED, surge multiplier 1.0 read from that artifact): recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 × 32.00 + 0.28 × 40.1) × 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP = 39.828. Refund = charged_total 43.41 − 39.828 = 3.582, rounded up to SGD 3.60. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and far below 90% of the charge, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S NO_ACTION ARGUMENT IS REJECTED. It is correct that 2.17 km (6.8%) of excess remains against the adjusted optimal, but POL-RD-01 establishes the deviation on the trip as driven against the booked optimal (7.07 km, 26.09%), and POL-RD-03 expressly refunds the excess beyond its cap under POL-RD-02 against the adjusted route. The 2.17 km the driver drove beyond what the closure justifies is the driver's own responsibility, not the rider's.\n\nTHE RIDER'S CLAIM OF ABOUT $14 IS NOT SUPPORTED. The rider is right that 34 km is far longer than her usual 27 km and that $43.41 is about $14 above her normal fare; but a documented closure justified 4.90 km of that excess, so only the excess beyond it is refunded.\n\nOTHER CLAIMS. POL-RD-04 moves no distance: the only route-proposing message is the driver's own ('accident on PIE after eunos, i go ECP instead ok'), and the rider's reply 'ok but not too long ah' names no road and carries no waypoint_hint, so there is no rider instruction to exclude distance for. The second advisory EV-ADVIS-00104-02 is impaired and that impairment is disclosed: weight 0.25, issue codes ADVISORY_UNCORROBORATED and UNVERIFIED_SOURCE; it is rejected on the merits because it describes a breakdown on the CTE between Ang Mo Kio Ave 1 and the SLE, a corridor this trip never enters, so it excuses nothing — and because it is present in the bundle and overlaps the trip window, POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged by it. No POL-RD-06 conduct referral arises: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against 288 completed trips in 90 days (ratio 0.0035, below 0.05), the excess is not material (7.07 km is under 8.0 km and 26.09% is under 50%), and the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is a context-only field under POL-GEN-01 that may not be substituted for the trailing-window figure named by POL-RD-06. POL-RD-09 adds nothing: there is no ERP, no airport surcharge on a trip originating at Tampines, and no unmatched charge line. POL-RD-11 does not apply because the fare model is METERED with no quoted fare.\n\nNO ESCALATION. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes (283 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, maximum gap 0.0 s), so the independent-corroboration requirement of POL-RD-07 does not arise and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged; trip identifiers match across the three artifacts, no timestamps conflict, the refund is far below SGD 150, and the second advisory is disposed of on the merits. The case is decided on the evidence, not held.\n\nThe monetary effect (SGD 3.60) is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so this provisional ruling executes on issue. Either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
