    "explanation": "Both of you: this is my ruling on trip TRP-00104 of 16 July 2026, Tampines (Our Tampines Hub) to one-north. The deviation was real, but the driver's explanation for most of it is good, so the rider gets a small refund, not the $14 she asked for.\n\n1. The measurement (POL-RD-01). The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00104, weight 1.0, 283 fixes, 10-second sampling, no gaps) records 34.17 km; the booked optimal route (EV-TRIP-00104) was 27.1 km. I use the trace figure, not the rounded 34.2 km copy, because POL-RD-01 says the trace governs. The excess is 7.07 km, or 26.09% of the optimal. Both POL-RD-01 tests pass (over 20%, over 0.8 km), so the deviation is established. It is not MATERIAL (under 50% and under 8.0 km), so no POL-RD-06 uplift or conduct referral follows from it.\n\n2. The driver's partial excuse (POL-RD-03). The LTA DataMall advisory EV-ADVIS-00104-01 (COMPLETE, weight 1.0) names the PIE towards Tuas after Eunos, which is the expressway the booked optimal route uses; its window 20:02-21:35 straddles the 20:35-21:22 trip; and the trace leaves the PIE at Bedok North Ave 4 before the blocked segment and rejoins on the AYE. That satisfies POL-RD-03. The exoneration is capped: justified excess = min(7.07, 1.30 x (30.1 - 27.1) + 1.00) = 4.90 km, giving a closure-adjusted optimal of 32.00 km at 40.1 minutes. So 4.90 km of the 7.07 km is excused; the remaining 2.17 km is not.\n\n3. The driver's NO_ACTION submission is refused. The argument that, measured against the adjusted 32.00 km, the remaining 2.17 km is only 6.8% and so fails POL-RD-01, leaving nothing payable, is rejected. The deviation is established on the excess as driven from the booked optimal, and POL-RD-03 itself directs that the excess beyond its cap 'is not exonerated and is refunded under POL-RD-02 computed against the closure-adjusted optimal route'. To let the establishment test swallow that direction would make the cap and the adjusted-route refund dead letters. The driver is not penalised for avoiding the closure; he accounts for the 2.17 km driven beyond even the capped allowance.\n\n4. The driver's CTE breakdown excuse fails. EV-ADVIS-00104-02 is impaired (weight_multiplier 0.25; issue codes ADVISORY_UNCORROBORATED, UNVERIFIED_SOURCE), and in any case it describes the CTE between Ang Mo Kio Ave 1 and the SLE, a corridor this trip never enters (intersects_route false; no fix inside its box). POL-RD-03(a) is not met, so it excuses nothing. Because it is present in the pool and its window covers the trip, its rejection is on the merits and is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation; it simply carries no weight under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13. The finding does not rest on that artifact, so its discount does not lower confidence.\n\n5. The rider's further points. The ECP/MCE/AYE route was not rider-requested: the only route proposal in the chat log (EV-CHAT-00104) is the driver's own ('accident on PIE after eunos, i go ECP instead ok') and the rider's 'ok but not too long ah' is an acknowledgment, not an instruction with a road or waypoint, so no distance is excluded under POL-RD-04. POL-RD-11 does not apply: the fare model on EV-FARE-00104 is METERED with no quoted fare. No corroboration condition attaches to the rider: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 1, well below the four-claim trigger in POL-RD-08.\n\n6. The money (POL-RD-02), computed against the closure-adjusted optimal route: recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 32.00 + 0.28 x 40.1) x 1.0 (surge read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier on EV-FARE-00104) + 0.80 platform fee = 39.828. charged_total = 43.41. Refund = 43.41 - 39.828 = 3.582, rounded up to 3.60. That is above the 0.50 de minimis and far below 90% of the charge, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND of $3.60.\n\n7. Nothing else moves. There are no ERP or toll lines and no airport surcharge on this trip (EV-FARE-00104), so POL-RD-09 adds no pass-through correction and produces no billing-integrity referral; the driver's own POL-RD-09 claim was discarded for not disclosing the impairment of the advisory it cited. No POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral arises (deviation_flags_90d is 1 against 288 completed trips - no pattern). No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trip identifier TRP-00104 matches across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; the trace is unimpaired for policy purposes (10-second sampling, zero gaps); no timestamps conflict; and no charge line is unmatched.\n\n8. Confidence 0.90, capped by the weight 1.0 of the artifacts that carry the decision (EV-GPS-00104, EV-TRIP-00104, EV-FARE-00104, EV-ADVIS-00104-01). The $3.60 refund is at or below the $8.00 automatic-execution threshold and is executed on issue; fare_breakdown.payment_status stays CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is set to 3.60. Either party may appeal once, within 30 days, through the help channel."
  },
