    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver. Outcome: the rider is refunded SGD 3.60 of the SGD 43.41 charged (PARTIAL_REFUND). The charge stands in every other respect.\n\n1. The trace and the excess. GPS trace EV-GPS-00104 is complete — 283 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s — so it is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) and no escalation arises under POL-RD-10(3). The governing measurement is the trace distance 34.17 km (POL-RD-01), not the rounded 34.2 km convenience copy on the trip record. Against the booked optimal of 27.1 km on EV-TRIP-00104 the excess is 7.07 km, or 26.09%; both POL-RD-01 establishment tests pass (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so a deviation is established on this trip's own telemetry. The rider's burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged: trip id TRP-00104 matches across trip record, trace and fare breakdown, and the trace's first fix at 20:35:10 matches the recorded start.\n\n2. The closure excuses part of it. LTA DataMall advisory EV-ADVIS-00104-01 (COMPLETE, weight 1.0) names the PIE towards Tuas after Eunos Link — a road the booked optimal route uses — with a 20:02–21:35 window covering the trip, and the trace leaves the PIE at Bedok North Ave 4 ahead of the blocked segment and rejoins on the AYE. POL-RD-03 therefore applies. The cap is min(7.07, 1.30 × (30.1 − 27.1) + 1.00) = 4.90 km, so 4.90 km of the 7.07 km is excused and the driver is not penalised for avoiding a HIGH-severity closure.\n\n3. Why NO_ACTION is not the outcome. The driver's advocate argues that once the closure-adjusted optimal of 32.00 km is used, the residual excess of 2.17 km is only 6.8% and fails POL-RD-01's percentage limb, so nothing is payable. I do not accept that. The deviation is established on the trace's measured excess against the booked optimal; POL-RD-02 applies where a deviation is established and no exculpatory clause FULLY excuses it, and POL-RD-03 excuses only 4.90 of the 7.07 km; and POL-RD-03 itself directs that the excess beyond the cap is not exonerated and is refunded under POL-RD-02 computed against the closure-adjusted optimal route. The adjusted optimal is the figure the refund is computed on, not a device that erases the deviation. Both advocates in fact agree the arithmetic lands at SGD 3.60.\n\n4. The arithmetic. fare_model is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so POL-RD-02 governs and POL-RD-11 does not apply. With the closure-adjusted optimal route of 32.00 km and 40.1 minutes (the booked 34.0 minutes scaled by 32.00/27.1, the amended duration being null), and the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from the fare breakdown EV-FARE-00104: recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 × 32.00 + 0.28 × 40.1) × 1.0 + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP = 39.828. Refund = charged_total 43.41 − 39.828 = 3.582, rounded up to SGD 3.60. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, and at 8.25% of the charge it is far below the 90% that would convert it to a full refund. The rider's SGD 14.00 is her estimate of the difference from her usual fare; the figure the record supports is SGD 3.60.\n\n5. Claims answered. (a) The driver's account that the diversion was occasioned by the closure is accepted so far as the capped 4.90 km goes, carried by EV-ADVIS-00104-01. (b) The chat log does not move money to the driver or excuse distance: the only route proposal in EV-CHAT-00104 is the driver's own message at 20:38:12, and the rider's reply 'ok but not too long ah' names no road and carries no waypoint_hint, so POL-RD-04(a) and (c) are not met and no distance is excluded on that ground. (c) The CTE advisory EV-ADVIS-00104-02 is impaired (weight 0.25, issue codes ADVISORY_UNCORROBORATED and UNVERIFIED_SOURCE) and describes a corridor this trip never enters; it excuses nothing, and because an advisory for this trip is on file and relied on, POL-RD-13 confirms this is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. (d) No POL-RD-06 conduct referral or uplift: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 against 288 completed trips in 90 days, so no pattern is established, and the excess (7.07 km / 26.09%) is below both materiality gates (8.0 km / 50%); the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and forms no part of this decision. (e) No billing-integrity referral: EV-FARE-00104 carries no ERP lines and no airport surcharge, and no charge line lacks a counterpart in the trace or trip record. (f) No POL-RD-10 trigger fires — the three artifacts carry matching trip identifiers, the trace is unimpaired, no timestamps conflict, the refund is far below SGD 150, and no charge line is unmatched — so the case is ruled on the merits.\n\n6. Discarded material. One claim on the driver's side was discarded by the citation referee and is recorded below; it is not a ground of this ruling.\n\n7. Confidence, referral and execution. Confidence is 0.9, capped by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding facts (EV-GPS-00104, EV-TRIP-00104, EV-ADVIS-00104-01 and EV-FARE-00104). No clause produces a referral. The refund of SGD 3.60 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically on issue; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
